# Contributing to {{ project_name }}

Issues and {{ pr }}s are welcome. [README.md](README.md) explains the project, and [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) holds the rules every change follows, for people and coding agents alike. Report a vulnerability privately instead, as [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md) says. Everyone taking part follows the [Code of Conduct](CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md); [GOVERNANCE.md](GOVERNANCE.md) says who decides what, and [ROADMAP.md](ROADMAP.md) where the project is going. Issues labeled `good first issue` are small, self-contained tasks for a first contribution.

## Prerequisites

- Git, and PowerShell 7 (`pwsh`): every command here runs from the repository root in PowerShell 7.
{%- if stack == 'dotnet' %}
- The .NET SDK that [global.json](global.json) selects, and the runtime of each older .NET a test project targets, which `./build/Get-TestRuntimes.ps1` names. `./build/Install-Dotnet.ps1` installs both beside the .NET that runs `dotnet`, or into the folder `-InstallDir` names; run it as an administrator, or with `sudo`, when .NET is installed system-wide.
{%- elif stack == 'python' %}
- Python 3 with pytest: `python -m pip install pytest pytest-cov`, then `python -m pip install -r requirements.txt` or `python -m pip install -e .` when the project has a `requirements.txt` or a `pyproject.toml`.
{%- elif stack == 'node' %}
- {% if pm == 'bun' %}Bun{% else %}Node.js LTS and {{ pm }}{% endif %}.
{%- if pm in ['pnpm', 'yarn'] %} Corepack runs the {{ pm }} version that `package.json`'s `packageManager` field names: `npm install --global corepack@latest`, then `corepack enable {{ pm }}`.
{%- endif %} Install the dependencies with {% if pm == 'pnpm' %}`pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`{% elif pm == 'yarn' %}`yarn install`{% elif pm == 'bun' %}`bun install --frozen-lockfile`{% else %}`npm ci`{% endif %}.
{%- elif stack == 'powershell' %}
- The Pester and PSScriptAnalyzer modules: `Install-Module Pester, PSScriptAnalyzer -Scope CurrentUser`.
{%- else %}
- The tools the build and test commands below run.
{%- endif %}
- On Windows, `git config --global core.longpaths true`, once: a plan's worktree under `.claude/worktrees/` can pass Windows' 260-character path limit.

## Set Up

Once in each clone, run `git config core.hooksPath .githooks`. It turns on `.githooks/pre-push`, which refuses a push to the default branch when the Landing section of `AGENTS.md` says `protect: hook`. When the clone already runs another tool's hooks, such as pre-commit, leave its hooks path alone.

